{
  "id": "field-research",
  "term": "field research",
  "definition": "Field research is research carried out in real-world community or local settings rather than only from a distance, often requiring direct contact with people and work in the places where they live. In this context, it involves practical and ethical demands such as reaching remote locations, obtaining informed consent, and building respectful dialogue with communities.",
